    "problemStatement": "For a sequence A=(A1,A2,…,AN)A = (A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_N)A=(A1​,A2​,…,AN​), we define f(A)f(A)f(A) in the following way:\n\n\nLet Pi=gcd⁡(A1,A2,…,Ai)P_i = \\gcd(A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_i)Pi​=gcd(A1​,A2​,…,Ai​)\nf(A)=f(A) = f(A)= number of indices iii (2≤i≤N2 \\le i \\le N2≤i≤N) such that Pi≠Pi−1P_i \\ne P_{i - 1}Pi​=Pi−1​.\nGiven an integer MMM, define g(N)g(N)g(N) as the **expected value** of f(A)f(A)f(A) when AAA is uniformly randomly selected among all MNM^NMN arrays satisfying the following conditions:\n\n\n∣A∣=N|A| = N∣A∣=N\n1≤Ai≤M1 \\le A_i \\le M1≤Ai​≤M\nFind lim⁡N→∞g(N)\\lim_{N \\to \\infty} g(N)limN→∞​g(N) modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\nFormally, it can be proven that this limit both exists and is a rational number of the form PQ\\frac{P}{Q}QP​ where Qmod  998244353≠0Q \\mod 998244353 \\ne 0Qmod998244353=0. You should print the unique integer RRR (0≤R&lt;9982443530 \\le R &lt; 9982443530≤R&lt;998244353) such that R⋅Q=P( mod R \\cdot Q = P (\\bmodR⋅Q=P(mod 998244353)998244353)998244353)\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first and only line of each test case contains a single integer MMM.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the value of lim⁡N→∞g(N)\\lim_{N \\to \\infty} g(N)limN→∞​g(N) modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
